<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34045" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">passīvus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		patior, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>capable of feeling</i> or <i>suffering</i>, <i>passible</i>, <i>passive</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anima passiva et interibilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 65</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr. p.
			49</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic., in gram., <i>passive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verbum passivum . . . quod habet naturam
					patiendi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 6, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Charis. 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Diom. 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Prisc. 8</span></i> et saep.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pas-sīvē</span></b> , <i>passively</i>, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Prisc. p.
			791</span></i> P.</div>
